 "id": "rise-of-the-guptas-319",
 "name": "The Rise of the Guptas",
 "era": "Magadha and its neighbours · from 319 CE",
 "disclaimer": "Loosely based on the founding of the Gupta empire under Chandragupta I and Samudragupta. Town positions are real; borders, armies and events are simplified or invented, and the dates of these kingdoms are uncertain.",
 "briefing": "Chandragupta I has taken the title Maharajadhiraja and holds Magadha, ruling from Pataliputra along the Ganga to Saketa and Prayaga. His marriage to the Licchavi princess Kumaradevi makes the Licchavis of Vaishali your allies. Around you, Aryavarta is divided: the Naga kings hold Padmavati, Mathura and Vidisha; Achyuta rules Ahichchhatra; the Yaudheya, Madraka and Malava republics guard the west; the Saka satraps hold Ujjayini; the Kushans rule beyond the Indus; Vanga holds Bengal and the Vakatakas the Deccan. Take every rival capital to make the Guptas paramount. Lose Pataliputra and the dynasty ends.",
 "victory": "Every rival capital bows to Pataliputra. The Guptas are paramount in Aryavarta.",
 "defeat": "Pataliputra has fallen. The Gupta line ends before it began.",
